# Motion

Every component that opens, closes, selects, switches or is pressed animates. HeroUI (heroui.com/docs) is the reference for feel: quick, light, and always tied to what the user did. Navigation is the worked example (`components/navigation`, section Motion).

## Tokens

Timing, easing, scale and distance come from `styles/foundations.css`. The shared keyframes live there too: `motion-fade-in`, `motion-fade-out`, `motion-rise-in`, `motion-pop-in`, `motion-pop-out`, `motion-bounce`.

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.menu { transition: opacity 0.2s ease; transform: scale(0.95); }

/* ✅ GOOD */
.menu[data-entering] { animation: motion-pop-in var(--motion-popover) var(--ease-standard); }
.menu[data-exiting] { animation: motion-pop-out var(--motion-popover-exit) var(--ease-exit) forwards; }
```

## Patterns

- Press: `transform: scale(var(--motion-press-scale))` on `:active` for every button-like control, in `--motion-instant`.
- Popover, menu, dropdown, tooltip: zoom from `--motion-pop-scale` and fade in with `--motion-popover`. Close with `--motion-popover-exit` on `--ease-exit`. Set `transform-origin` to the trigger side and flip it in RTL.
- Toggle presence with `data-entering` and `data-exiting`, then `hidden` after `animationend`, as in `presence()` in `components/navigation/navigation.js`. Never flip `hidden` alone on something the user opened.
- Selection that moves (sidebar item, tab, segment): one indicator slides between items on `--motion-indicator` with `--ease-spring`. Do not fade per-item backgrounds.
- Drawers and sheets: enter on `--motion-drawer` or `--motion-sheet`, exit faster on the matching `-exit` token with `--ease-exit`. Scrims use `--motion-backdrop-exit` on close.
- Lists that appear: rows rise in with `motion-rise-in`, delayed by `--motion-stagger` per row, capped at about 4 steps.
- Content that swaps (page, tab panel): `motion-rise-in` on `--motion-standard`.
- Play entrances only on a user action. Mark the moment with a short-lived `data-motion` (see `cue()`); never replay on a repaint.
- If a component re-renders its DOM, keep the previous state, force a reflow, then flip, so transitions still run.

## Rules

- Animate `transform` and `opacity` only, plus colour and shadow transitions. Never animate width, height, top or left on content.
- Exits are faster than entrances. No animation longer than `--motion-sheet`.
- Reduce Motion: `prefers-reduced-motion` and `data-reduce-motion="true"` already turn movement into a 200 ms fade through the tokens. Do not hardcode durations that skip this. A sliding indicator jumps.
- Arabic and RTL: slide directions and transform origins mirror.

## Platforms

Specify motion for all three platforms with the same meaning and tokens.

- Web: the CSS above.
- iOS: SwiftUI `.spring(duration:bounce:)` from the token duration (bounce 0 for standard, 0.2 for `--ease-spring`), system presentations for sheets and popovers, `.symbolEffect(.bounce)` for tab icons, `accessibilityReduceMotion` for Reduce Motion.
- Android: Material 3 motion: emphasized easing for enter, emphasized accelerate for exit, shared axis and fade through for content, ripple for press. Honour the animator duration scale.
